WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.560
CI/CD compromise matters because applications often enforce identity, access,

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.380
data handling, business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.520
Teams should evaluate this issue across user-facing features, APIs, administrative tools,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.540
cloud services, and delivery pipelines.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.600
Unsigned code matters because applications often enforce identity, access, data handling,

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.460
business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:33.360
Insecure deserialization matters because applications often enforce identity, access,

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.420
data handling, business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:43.080
Build pipeline attacks matters because applications often enforce identity, access,

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.820
data handling, business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.800
